The attached image (Fig. 4) from the PDF demonstrates the enhanced uptake of antigens by dendritic cells (BMDCs) when formulated with Nano-11. Confocal microscopy shows minimal uptake of soluble FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA) by BMDCs. However, when OVA is adsorbed to AF647-labeled Nano-11, both nanoparticles and antigen are efficiently internalized and colocalized within nearly all BMDCs. This illustrates Nano-11's ability to significantly improve the delivery of negatively charged protein antigens into dendritic cells, supporting its role as an effective vaccine adjuvant.